<hr data-start=3D"1493" data-end=3D"1496">
<h2 data-start=3D"1498" data-end=3D"1553">=F0=9F=A7=A0 2. Introduction aux =
mots-cl=C3=A9s de contr=C3=B4le de flux</h2>
<p data-start=3D"1555" data-end=3D"1820">En Java, les mots-cl=C3=A9s <stron=
g data-start=3D"1578" data-end=3D"1589"><code data-start=3D"1580" data-end=
=3D"1587">break</code></strong>, <strong data-start=3D"1591" data-end=3D"16=
05"><code data-start=3D"1593" data-end=3D"1603">continue</code></strong>, e=
t <strong data-start=3D"1610" data-end=3D"1622"><code data-start=3D"1612" d=
ata-end=3D"1620">return</code></strong> permettent de contr=C3=B4ler le flu=
x d'ex=C3=A9cution d'un programme de mani=C3=A8re pr=C3=A9cise. Ces mots-cl=
=C3=A9s agissent directement sur le comportement des boucles ou des fonctio=
ns. Voici un aper=C3=A7u de leur utilit=C3=A9 :</p>
<ol data-start=3D"1822" data-end=3D"2119">
<li data-start=3D"1822" data-end=3D"1897">
<p data-start=3D"1825" data-end=3D"1897"><strong data-start=3D"1825" data-e=
nd=3D"1836"><code data-start=3D"1827" data-end=3D"1834">break</code></stron=
g> : Sert =C3=A0 sortir imm=C3=A9diatement d'une boucle ou d'un <code data-=
start=3D"1888" data-end=3D"1896">switch</code>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1898" data-end=3D"2026">
<p data-start=3D"1901" data-end=3D"2026"><strong data-start=3D"1901" data-e=
nd=3D"1915"><code data-start=3D"1903" data-end=3D"1913">continue</code></st=
rong> : Permet de passer =C3=A0 l'it=C3=A9ration suivante d'une boucle, en =
sautant le reste du code dans l=E2=80=99it=C3=A9ration en cours.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2027" data-end=3D"2119">
<p data-start=3D"2030" data-end=3D"2119"><strong data-start=3D"2030" data-e=
nd=3D"2042"><code data-start=3D"2032" data-end=3D"2040">return</code></stro=
ng> : Utilis=C3=A9 dans une m=C3=A9thode pour renvoyer une valeur et sortir=
 de la m=C3=A9thode.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<hr data-start=3D"2121" data-end=3D"2124">
<h2 data-start=3D"2126" data-end=3D"2152">=E2=9A=A1 3. Le mot-cl=C3=A9 <cod=
e data-start=3D"2145" data-end=3D"2152">break</code></h2>
<h3 data-start=3D"2154" data-end=3D"2187">3.1 Syntaxe et fonctionnement</h3=
>
<p data-start=3D"2189" data-end=3D"2469">Le mot-cl=C3=A9 <strong data-start=
=3D"2200" data-end=3D"2211"><code data-start=3D"2202" data-end=3D"2209">bre=
ak</code></strong> est principalement utilis=C3=A9 pour sortir d'une boucle=
 (<code data-start=3D"2265" data-end=3D"2270">for</code>, <code data-start=
=3D"2272" data-end=3D"2279">while</code>, <code data-start=3D"2281" data-en=
d=3D"2291">do-while</code>) ou d=E2=80=99un <strong data-start=3D"2301" dat=
a-end=3D"2313"><code data-start=3D"2303" data-end=3D"2311">switch</code></s=
trong> avant que la condition de la boucle ne soit fausse. D=C3=A8s que le =
<code data-start=3D"2377" data-end=3D"2384">break</code> est rencontr=C3=A9=
, l'ex=C3=A9cution du programme quitte imm=C3=A9diatement la structure conc=
ern=C3=A9e.</p>
