ts en <code data-start=3D"6062" data-end=3D"6071">private</code>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6073" data-end=3D"6130">
<p data-start=3D"6075" data-end=3D"6130">Fournir uniquement les getters/set=
ters <strong data-start=3D"6114" data-end=3D"6129">n=C3=A9cessaires</strong=
>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6131" data-end=3D"6170">
<p data-start=3D"6133" data-end=3D"6170">Valider les entr=C3=A9es dans les =
setters.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6171" data-end=3D"6228">
<p data-start=3D"6173" data-end=3D"6228">Utiliser des noms clairs : <code d=
ata-start=3D"6200" data-end=3D"6210">getNom()</code>, <code data-start=3D"6=
212" data-end=3D"6222">setAge()</code>, etc.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6229" data-end=3D"6299">
<p data-start=3D"6231" data-end=3D"6299">Pour les objets immuables (ex : <c=
ode data-start=3D"6263" data-end=3D"6271">String</code>), ne pas fournir de=
 setter.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6300" data-end=3D"6379">
<p data-start=3D"6302" data-end=3D"6379">=C3=89viter les setters si l=E2=80=
=99=C3=A9tat ne doit pas changer (<code data-start=3D"6352" data-end=3D"635=
9">final</code>, objets constants).</p>
</li>
</ul>
