<hr data-start=3D"5557" data-end=3D"5560">
<h2 data-start=3D"5562" data-end=3D"5604">4. =F0=9F=A7=91=E2=80=8D=F0=9F=92=
=BB R=C3=A8gles d=E2=80=99accessibilit=C3=A9 en Java</h2>
<h3 data-start=3D"5606" data-end=3D"5629">Acc=C3=A8s aux classes :</h3>
<ul data-start=3D"5630" data-end=3D"5913">
<li data-start=3D"5630" data-end=3D"5706">
<p data-start=3D"5632" data-end=3D"5706"><strong data-start=3D"5632" data-e=
nd=3D"5642">Public</strong> : La classe est accessible depuis n=E2=80=99imp=
orte quel autre fichier.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"5707" data-end=3D"5798">
<p data-start=3D"5709" data-end=3D"5798"><strong data-start=3D"5709" data-e=
nd=3D"5738">Package-private (default)</strong> : La classe est accessible u=
niquement dans le m=C3=AAme package.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"5799" data-end=3D"5913">
<p data-start=3D"5801" data-end=3D"5913"><strong data-start=3D"5801" data-e=
nd=3D"5812">Private</strong> : Les classes internes =C3=A0 une autre classe=
 ne peuvent =C3=AAtre accessibles qu'=C3=A0 l=E2=80=99int=C3=A9rieur de la =
classe.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start=3D"5915" data-end=3D"5938">Acc=C3=A8s aux membres :</h3>
<ul data-start=3D"5939" data-end=3D"6149">
<li data-start=3D"5939" data-end=3D"5968">
<p data-start=3D"5941" data-end=3D"5968"><strong data-start=3D"5941" data-e=
nd=3D"5951">Public</strong> : Acc=C3=A8s partout.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"5969" data-end=3D"6023">
<p data-start=3D"5971" data-end=3D"6023"><strong data-start=3D"5971" data-e=
nd=3D"5982">Private</strong> : Acc=C3=A8s uniquement au sein de la classe.<=
/p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6024" data-end=3D"6094">
<p data-start=3D"6026" data-end=3D"6094"><strong data-start=3D"6026" data-e=
nd=3D"6039">Protected</strong> : Acc=C3=A8s dans le m=C3=AAme package et da=
ns les sous-classes.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6095" data-end=3D"6149">
<p data-start=3D"6097" data-end=3D"6149"><strong data-start=3D"6097" data-e=
nd=3D"6108">Default</strong> : Acc=C3=A8s uniquement dans le m=C3=AAme pack=
age.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"6151" data-end=3D"6154">
<h2 data-start=3D"6156" data-end=3D"6181">5. =F0=9F=93=A6 Packages en Java<=
/h2>
<p data-start=3D"6183" data-end=3D"6305">Un <strong data-start=3D"6186" dat=
a-end=3D"6197">package</strong> en Java est un m=C3=A9canisme qui permet d=
=E2=80=99organiser des classes et des interfaces. Les packages permettent d=
e :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"6307" data-end=3D"6508">
<li data-start=3D"6307" data-end=3D"6362">
<p data-start=3D"6309" data-end=3D"6362">G=C3=A9rer des namespaces pour =C3=
=A9viter les conflits de nom.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6363" data-end=3D"6431">
<p data-start=3D"6365" data-end=3D"6431">Organiser logiquement les classes =
dans des r=C3=A9pertoires (dossiers).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6432" data-end=3D"6508">
<p data-start=3D"6434" data-end=3D"6508">Restreindre l=E2=80=99acc=C3=A8s =
=C3=A0 des classes en les cachant dans des packages priv=C3=A9s.</p>
</li>
</ul>
