<p data-start=3D"1298" data-end=3D"1314">&lt;a name=3D"1"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;</p>
<h2 data-start=3D"1315" data-end=3D"1357">1. =F0=9F=94=8D Introduction aux =
Pools de Threads</h2>
<p data-start=3D"1359" data-end=3D"1714">En programmation <strong data-star=
t=3D"1376" data-end=3D"1393">multithread=C3=A9e</strong>, plusieurs threads=
 peuvent =C3=AAtre utilis=C3=A9s pour ex=C3=A9cuter des t=C3=A2ches simulta=
n=C3=A9ment, ce qui am=C3=A9liore la r=C3=A9activit=C3=A9 et les performanc=
es. Cependant, <strong data-start=3D"1537" data-end=3D"1559">g=C3=A9rer man=
uellement</strong> ces threads peut rapidement devenir complexe, surtout lo=
rsqu'il faut =C3=A9viter les <strong data-start=3D"1640" data-end=3D"1661">=
fuites de m=C3=A9moire</strong>, les <strong data-start=3D"1667" data-end=
=3D"1679">blocages</strong> ou les <strong data-start=3D"1687" data-end=3D"=
1713">goulots d'=C3=A9tranglement</strong>.</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"1716" data-end=3D"1757">Qu'est-ce qu'un <strong data-star=
t=3D"1736" data-end=3D"1755">Pool de Threads</strong> ?</h3>
<p data-start=3D"1758" data-end=3D"2075">Un <strong data-start=3D"1761" dat=
a-end=3D"1780">pool de threads</strong> est une <strong data-start=3D"1789"=
 data-end=3D"1828">collection de threads r=C3=A9utilisables</strong>, g=C3=
=A9r=C3=A9e par un <strong data-start=3D"1843" data-end=3D"1867">gestionnai=
re de pool</strong> (typiquement un <code data-start=3D"1884" data-end=3D"1=
901">ExecutorService</code> en Java). Plut=C3=B4t que de cr=C3=A9er un nouv=
eau thread pour chaque t=C3=A2che, on r=C3=A9cup=C3=A8re un thread existant=
 dans le pool, ce qui permet de r=C3=A9utiliser les ressources plus efficac=
ement.</p>
<blockquote data-start=3D"2077" data-end=3D"2221">
<p data-start=3D"2079" data-end=3D"2221">Le <strong data-start=3D"2082" dat=
a-end=3D"2097">Thread Pool</strong> am=C3=A9liore la <strong data-start=3D"=
2110" data-end=3D"2139">gestion de la concurrence</strong> en limitant la c=
r=C3=A9ation excessive de threads et en optimisant leur r=C3=A9utilisation.=
</p>
</blockquote>
<hr data-start=3D"2223" data-end=3D"2226">
<p data-start=3D"2228" data-end=3D"2244">&lt;a name=3D"2"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;</p>
<h2 data-start=3D"2245" data-end=3D"2294">2. =F0=9F=A7=A0 Pourquoi utiliser=
 des Pools de Threads ?</h2>
<ol data-start=3D"2296" data-end=3D"2816">
<li data-start=3D"2296" data-end=3D"2427">
<p data-start=3D"2299" data-end=3D"2427"><strong data-start=3D"2299" data-e=
nd=3D"2322">R=C3=A9duction des co=C3=BBts</strong> : Cr=C3=A9er et d=C3=A9t=
ruire des threads est une op=C3=A9ration co=C3=BBteuse. Les pools r=C3=A9ut=
ilisent les threads existants.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2428" data-end=3D"2550">
<p data-start=3D"2431" data-end=3D"2550"><strong data-start=3D"2431" data-e=
nd=3D"2461">Contr=C3=B4le de la concurrence</strong> : Limite le nombre de =
threads en cours d'ex=C3=A9cution pour =C3=A9viter une surcharge du syst=C3=
=A8me.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2551" data-end=3D"2685">
<p data-start=3D"2554" data-end=3D"2685"><strong data-start=3D"2554" data-e=
nd=3D"2590">Meilleure gestion des ressources</strong> : =C3=89vite la cr=C3=
=A9ation excessive de threads en fonction de la capacit=C3=A9 du syst=C3=A8=
me (CPU, m=C3=A9moire).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2686" data-end=3D"2816">
<p data-start=3D"2689" data-end=3D"2816"><strong data-start=3D"2689" data-e=
nd=3D"2723">Am=C3=A9lioration de la performance</strong> : R=C3=A9duire la =
surcharge de gestion des threads permet d'ex=C3=A9cuter plus de t=C3=A2ches=
 efficacement.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<hr data-start=3D"2818" data-end=3D"2821">
<p data-start=3D"2823" data-end=3D"2839">&lt;a name=3D"3"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;</p>
<h2 data-start=3D"2840" data-end=3D"2863">3. =F0=9F=8F=97=EF=B8=8F Concepts=
 cl=C3=A9s</h2>
<h3 data-start=3D"2865" data-end=3D"2886"><code data-start=3D"2869" data-en=
d=3D"2886">ExecutorService</code></h3>
<p data-start=3D"2887" data-end=3D"3161">L'interface <strong data-start=3D"=
2899" data-end=3D"2920"><code data-start=3D"2901" data-end=3D"2918">Executo=
rService</code></strong> dans <code data-start=3D"2926" data-end=3D"2948">j=
ava.util.concurrent</code> est utilis=C3=A9e pour g=C3=A9rer un pool de thr=
eads. Elle fournit des m=C3=A9thodes pour soumettre des t=C3=A2ches et r=C3=
=A9cup=C3=A9rer les r=C3=A9sultats. Elle offre =C3=A9galement un moyen de g=
=C3=A9rer le cycle de vie du pool (d=C3=A9marrage, arr=C3=AAt, etc.).</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"3163" data-end=3D"3187"><code data-start=3D"3167" data-en=
d=3D"3187">ThreadPoolExecutor</code></h3>
<p data-start=3D"3188" data-end=3D"3358">La classe <strong data-start=3D"31=
98" data-end=3D"3222"><code data-start=3D"3200" data-end=3D"3220">ThreadPoo=
lExecutor</code></strong> est l'impl=C3=A9mentation de <code data-start=3D"=
3247" data-end=3D"3264">ExecutorService</code>. Elle g=C3=A8re un pool de t=
hreads avec une configuration personnalis=C3=A9e, permettant de contr=C3=B4=
ler :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"3360" data-end=3D"3528">
<li data-start=3D"3360" data-end=3D"3407">
<p data-start=3D"3362" data-end=3D"3407">Le nombre de threads de base (<cod=
e data-start=3D"3392" data-end=3D"3406">corePoolSize</code>)</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3408" data-end=3D"3458">
<p data-start=3D"3410" data-end=3D"3458">Le nombre maximum de threads (<cod=
e data-start=3D"3440" data-end=3D"3457">maximumPoolSize</code>)</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3459" data-end=3D"3528">
<p data-start=3D"3461" data-end=3D"3528">Le temps avant la destruction d'un=
 thread inactif (<code data-start=3D"3512" data-end=3D"3527">keepAliveTime<=
/code>)</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start=3D"3530" data-end=3D"3545"><code data-start=3D"3534" data-en=
d=3D"3545">Executors</code></h3>
<p data-start=3D"3546" data-end=3D"3668">La classe <strong data-start=3D"35=
56" data-end=3D"3571"><code data-start=3D"3558" data-end=3D"3569">Executors=
</code></strong> offre des m=C3=A9thodes statiques pour cr=C3=A9er diff=C3=
=A9rents types de pools de threads pr=C3=A9d=C3=A9finis, comme :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"3670" data-end=3D"3779">
<li data-start=3D"3670" data-end=3D"3694">
<p data-start=3D"3672" data-end=3D"3694"><code data-start=3D"3672" data-end=
=3D"3694">newFixedThreadPool()</code></p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3695" data-end=3D"3720">
<p data-start=3D"3697" data-end=3D"3720"><code data-start=3D"3697" data-end=
=3D"3720">newCachedThreadPool()</code></p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3721" data-end=3D"3750">
<p data-start=3D"3723" data-end=3D"3750"><code data-start=3D"3723" data-end=
=3D"3750">newSingleThreadExecutor()</code></p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3751" data-end=3D"3779">
<p data-start=3D"3753" data-end=3D"3779"><code data-start=3D"3753" data-end=
=3D"3779">newScheduledThreadPool()</code></p>
</li>
</ul>
