<p data-start=3D"7091" data-end=3D"7107">&lt;a name=3D"5"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;</p>
<h2 data-start=3D"7108" data-end=3D"7146">5. =F0=9F=94=91 R=C3=A9daction de=
 Tests avec JUnit</h2>
<h3 data-start=3D"7148" data-end=3D"7193">Bonnes Pratiques pour R=C3=A9dige=
r des Tests :</h3>
<ol data-start=3D"7194" data-end=3D"7710">
<li data-start=3D"7194" data-end=3D"7298">
<p data-start=3D"7197" data-end=3D"7298"><strong data-start=3D"7197" data-e=
nd=3D"7211">Simplicit=C3=A9</strong> : Un test doit =C3=AAtre simple, ind=
=C3=A9pendant et se concentrer sur une seule fonctionnalit=C3=A9.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"7299" data-end=3D"7416">
<p data-start=3D"7302" data-end=3D"7416"><strong data-start=3D"7302" data-e=
nd=3D"7315">Isolation</strong> : Les tests doivent =C3=AAtre ind=C3=A9penda=
nts les uns des autres, et ne pas d=C3=A9pendre de l=E2=80=99ordre d=E2=80=
=99ex=C3=A9cution.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"7417" data-end=3D"7567">
<p data-start=3D"7420" data-end=3D"7567"><strong data-start=3D"7420" data-e=
nd=3D"7456">Utilisation d'assertions claires</strong> : Utilisez des assert=
ions explicites comme <code data-start=3D"7500" data-end=3D"7514">assertEqu=
als</code>, <code data-start=3D"7516" data-end=3D"7528">assertTrue</code>, =
etc., pour rendre vos tests lisibles.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"7568" data-end=3D"7710">
<p data-start=3D"7571" data-end=3D"7710"><strong data-start=3D"7571" data-e=
nd=3D"7595">Nomination des tests</strong> : Nommez vos tests de mani=C3=A8r=
e =C3=A0 ce qu=E2=80=99ils d=C3=A9crivent ce qu=E2=80=99ils testent. Exempl=
e : <code data-start=3D"7677" data-end=3D"7709">shouldAddTwoNumbersCorrectl=
y()</code>.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<h3 data-start=3D"7712" data-end=3D"7746">Types d=E2=80=99assertions couran=
tes :</h3>
<ul data-start=3D"7747" data-end=3D"8092">
<li data-start=3D"7747" data-end=3D"7829">
<p data-start=3D"7749" data-end=3D"7829"><strong data-start=3D"7749" data-e=
nd=3D"7785"><code data-start=3D"7751" data-end=3D"7783">assertEquals(expect=
ed, actual)</code></strong> : V=C3=A9rifie que les deux valeurs sont =C3=A9=
gales.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"7830" data-end=3D"7897">
<p data-start=3D"7832" data-end=3D"7897"><strong data-start=3D"7832" data-e=
nd=3D"7859"><code data-start=3D"7834" data-end=3D"7857">assertTrue(conditio=
n)</code></strong> : V=C3=A9rifie que la condition est vraie.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"7898" data-end=3D"7967">
<p data-start=3D"7900" data-end=3D"7967"><strong data-start=3D"7900" data-e=
nd=3D"7928"><code data-start=3D"7902" data-end=3D"7926">assertFalse(conditi=
on)</code></strong> : V=C3=A9rifie que la condition est fausse.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"7968" data-end=3D"8025">
<p data-start=3D"7970" data-end=3D"8025"><strong data-start=3D"7970" data-e=
nd=3D"7994"><code data-start=3D"7972" data-end=3D"7992">assertNull(object)<=
/code></strong> : V=C3=A9rifie que l=E2=80=99objet est nul.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"8026" data-end=3D"8092">
<p data-start=3D"8028" data-end=3D"8092"><strong data-start=3D"8028" data-e=
nd=3D"8055"><code data-start=3D"8030" data-end=3D"8053">assertNotNull(objec=
t)</code></strong> : V=C3=A9rifie que l=E2=80=99objet n=E2=80=99est pas nul=
.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"8094" data-end=3D"8097">
<p data-start=3D"8099" data-end=3D"8115">&lt;a name=3D"6"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;</p>
