<h2 data-start=3D"1468" data-end=3D"1503">1. =F0=9F=94=B0 Introduction =C3=
=A0 JSP et JSTL</h2>
<h3 data-start=3D"1505" data-end=3D"1533">=E2=9C=85 JSP (JavaServer Pages)<=
/h3>
<ul data-start=3D"1535" data-end=3D"1811">
<li data-start=3D"1535" data-end=3D"1610">
<p data-start=3D"1537" data-end=3D"1610">Les JSP sont des <strong data-star=
t=3D"1554" data-end=3D"1596">pages HTML enrichies avec du code Java</strong=
> c=C3=B4t=C3=A9 serveur.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1611" data-end=3D"1745">
<p data-start=3D"1613" data-end=3D"1745">Elles permettent de <strong data-s=
tart=3D"1633" data-end=3D"1658">g=C3=A9n=C3=A9rer dynamiquement</strong> de=
s pages HTML =C3=A0 partir de donn=C3=A9es (base de donn=C3=A9es, param=C3=
=A8tres HTTP, sessions, etc.).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1746" data-end=3D"1811">
<p data-start=3D"1748" data-end=3D"1811">Remplacent (en partie) les Servlet=
s pour la g=C3=A9n=C3=A9ration de vues.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start=3D"1813" data-end=3D"1850">=E2=9C=85 JSTL (JSP Standard Tag =
Library)</h3>
<ul data-start=3D"1852" data-end=3D"2070">
<li data-start=3D"1852" data-end=3D"1977">
<p data-start=3D"1854" data-end=3D"1977">JSTL est une biblioth=C3=A8que de =
<strong data-start=3D"1883" data-end=3D"1908">balises standardis=C3=A9es</s=
trong> qui fournit des fonctions logiques, it=C3=A9ratives, formatage, SQL,=
 etc.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1978" data-end=3D"2070">
<p data-start=3D"1980" data-end=3D"2070">Permet d=E2=80=99<strong data-star=
t=3D"1989" data-end=3D"2029">=C3=A9viter d=E2=80=99=C3=A9crire du Java dans=
 les JSP</strong> : plus lisible, maintenable et s=C3=A9curis=C3=A9.</p>
</li>
</ul>
