nd=3D"1347">REST (Representational State Transfer)</strong> est un style d'=
architecture bas=C3=A9 sur :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"1387" data-end=3D"1673">
<li data-start=3D"1387" data-end=3D"1430">
<p data-start=3D"1389" data-end=3D"1430"><strong data-start=3D"1389" data-e=
nd=3D"1397">HTTP</strong> comme protocole de communication</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1431" data-end=3D"1497">
<p data-start=3D"1433" data-end=3D"1497"><strong data-start=3D"1433" data-e=
nd=3D"1447">Ressources</strong> identifi=C3=A9es par des URI (<code data-st=
art=3D"1473" data-end=3D"1481">/users</code>, <code data-start=3D"1483" dat=
a-end=3D"1496">/articles/1</code>)</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1498" data-end=3D"1673">
<p data-start=3D"1500" data-end=3D"1535">Utilisation des <strong data-start=
=3D"1516" data-end=3D"1533">m=C3=A9thodes HTTP</strong> :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"1538" data-end=3D"1673">
<li data-start=3D"1538" data-end=3D"1555">
<p data-start=3D"1540" data-end=3D"1555"><code data-start=3D"1540" data-end=
=3D"1545">GET</code> =E2=86=92 lecture</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1558" data-end=3D"1577">
<p data-start=3D"1560" data-end=3D"1577"><code data-start=3D"1560" data-end=
=3D"1566">POST</code> =E2=86=92 cr=C3=A9ation</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1580" data-end=3D"1610">
<p data-start=3D"1582" data-end=3D"1610"><code data-start=3D"1582" data-end=
=3D"1587">PUT</code> =E2=86=92 mise =C3=A0 jour compl=C3=A8te</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1613" data-end=3D"1646">
<p data-start=3D"1615" data-end=3D"1646"><code data-start=3D"1615" data-end=
=3D"1622">PATCH</code> =E2=86=92 mise =C3=A0 jour partielle</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1649" data-end=3D"1673">
<p data-start=3D"1651" data-end=3D"1673"><code data-start=3D"1651" data-end=
=3D"1659">DELETE</code> =E2=86=92 suppression</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"1675" data-end=3D"1719">Les REST APIs renvoient souvent du=
 <strong data-start=3D"1710" data-end=3D"1718">JSON</strong>.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"1721" data-end=3D"1724">
<p data-start=3D"1726" data-end=3D"1742">&lt;a name=3D"2"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;</p>
<h2 data-start=3D"1743" data-end=3D"1785">2. =F0=9F=A7=B1 Architecture REST=
ful et principes</h2>
<ul data-start=3D"1787" data-end=3D"2019">
<li data-start=3D"1787" data-end=3D"1836">
<p data-start=3D"1789" data-end=3D"1836"><strong data-start=3D"1789" data-e=
nd=3D"1802">Stateless</strong> : chaque requ=C3=AAte est ind=C3=A9pendante<=
/p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1837" data-end=3D"1885">
<p data-start=3D"1839" data-end=3D"1885"><strong data-start=3D"1839" data-e=
nd=3D"1860">Uniform Interface</strong> : conventions coh=C3=A9rentes</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1886" data-end=3D"1944">
<p data-start=3D"1888" data-end=3D"1944"><strong data-start=3D"1888" data-e=
nd=3D"1901">Cacheable</strong> : les r=C3=A9ponses peuvent =C3=AAtre mises =
en cache</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1945" data-end=3D"1986">
<p data-start=3D"1947" data-end=3D"1986"><strong data-start=3D"1947" data-e=
nd=3D"1965">Layered System</strong> : logique en couches</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1987" data-end=3D"2019">
<p data-start=3D"1989" data-end=3D"2019"><strong data-start=3D"1989" data-e=
nd=3D"2007">Code on demand</strong> (optionnel)</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"2021" data-end=3D"2024">
<p data-start=3D"2026" data-end=3D"2042">&lt;a name=3D"3"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;</p>
<h2 data-start=3D"2043" data-end=3D"2095">3. =E2=9A=99=EF=B8=8F Pr=C3=A9sen=
tation de Spring MVC dans Spring Boot</h2>
<p data-start=3D"2097" data-end=3D"2142">Spring MVC est le module de Spring=
 qui g=C3=A8re :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"2143" data-end=3D"2347">
<li data-start=3D"2143" data-end=3D"2185">
<p data-start=3D"2145" data-end=3D"2185">Les contr=C3=B4leurs HTTP (<code d=
ata-start=3D"2167" data-end=3D"2184">@RestController</code>)</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2186" data-end=3D"2245">
<p data-start=3D"2188" data-end=3D"2245">Le mapping d'URL (<code data-start=
=3D"2206" data-end=3D"2223">@RequestMapping</code>, <code data-start=3D"222=
5" data-end=3D"2238">@GetMapping</code>, etc.)</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2246" data-end=3D"2286">
<p data-start=3D"2248" data-end=3D"2286">La s=C3=A9rialisation JSON avec <s=
trong data-start=3D"2275" data-end=3D"2286">Jackson</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2287" data-end=3D"2347">
<p data-start=3D"2289" data-end=3D"2347">Le <strong data-start=3D"2292" dat=
a-end=3D"2303">binding</strong> de donn=C3=A9es entre les objets Java et le=
 JSON</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"2349" data-end=3D"2400"><strong data-start=3D"2349" data-e=
nd=3D"2364">Spring Boot</strong> facilite tout cela en fournissant :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"2401" data-end=3D"2531">
<li data-start=3D"2401" data-end=3D"2428">
<p data-start=3D"2403" data-end=3D"2428">Configuration automatique</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2429" data-end=3D"2478">
<p data-start=3D"2431" data-end=3D"2478">D=C3=A9marrage rapide (via <code d=
ata-start=3D"2453" data-end=3D"2477">@SpringBootApplication</code>)</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2479" data-end=3D"2531">
<p data-start=3D"2481" data-end=3D"2531">Int=C3=A9gration native avec Jacks=
on, Spring Data, etc.</p>
</li>
</ul>
