<hr data-start=3D"5455" data-end=3D"5458">
<p data-start=3D"5460" data-end=3D"5476">&lt;a name=3D"7"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;</p>
<h2 data-start=3D"5477" data-end=3D"5535">7. Gestion des erreurs en JDBC : =
exceptions et rollback</h2>
<h3 data-start=3D"5537" data-end=3D"5556">Types d=E2=80=99erreurs</h3>
<ul data-start=3D"5558" data-end=3D"5790">
<li data-start=3D"5558" data-end=3D"5629">
<p data-start=3D"5560" data-end=3D"5629"><strong data-start=3D"5560" data-e=
nd=3D"5576">SQLException</strong> : classe principale des exceptions li=C3=
=A9es =C3=A0 la base</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"5630" data-end=3D"5696">
<p data-start=3D"5632" data-end=3D"5696"><strong data-start=3D"5632" data-e=
nd=3D"5657">SQLTransientException</strong> : erreurs temporaires (ex : time=
out)</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"5697" data-end=3D"5790">
<p data-start=3D"5699" data-end=3D"5790"><strong data-start=3D"5699" data-e=
nd=3D"5743">SQLIntegrityConstraintViolationException</strong> : violation d=
e contraintes (ex : cl=C3=A9 unique)</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start=3D"5792" data-end=3D"5812">Bonnes pratiques</h3>
<ul data-start=3D"5814" data-end=3D"6117">
<li data-start=3D"5814" data-end=3D"5896">
<p data-start=3D"5816" data-end=3D"5896">Utiliser un bloc <code data-start=
=3D"5833" data-end=3D"5852">try-catch-finally</code> pour garantir la ferme=
ture des ressources</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"5897" data-end=3D"5983">
<p data-start=3D"5899" data-end=3D"5983">Sur exception, effectuer un <code =
data-start=3D"5927" data-end=3D"5939">rollback()</code> pour annuler les mo=
difications partielles</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"5984" data-end=3D"6050">
<p data-start=3D"5986" data-end=3D"6050">Journaliser l=E2=80=99erreur avec =
son SQLState, code d=E2=80=99erreur, message</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6051" data-end=3D"6117">
<p data-start=3D"6053" data-end=3D"6117">R=C3=A9initialiser l=E2=80=99=C3=
=A9tat auto-commit =C3=A0 <code data-start=3D"6088" data-end=3D"6094">true<=
/code> dans le bloc <code data-start=3D"6108" data-end=3D"6117">finally</co=
de></p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"6119" data-end=3D"6122">
<p data-start=3D"6124" data-end=3D"6140">&lt;a name=3D"8"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;</p>
<h2 data-start=3D"6141" data-end=3D"6198">8. Bonnes pratiques pour g=C3=A9r=
er transactions et erreurs</h2>
<ul data-start=3D"6200" data-end=3D"6782">
<li data-start=3D"6200" data-end=3D"6269">
<p data-start=3D"6202" data-end=3D"6269">Toujours d=C3=A9sactiver auto-comm=
it pour un groupe d=E2=80=99op=C3=A9rations li=C3=A9es</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6270" data-end=3D"6340">
<p data-start=3D"6272" data-end=3D"6340">Faire un commit <strong data-start=
=3D"6288" data-end=3D"6338">seulement si toutes les op=C3=A9rations r=C3=A9=
ussissent</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6341" data-end=3D"6386">
<p data-start=3D"6343" data-end=3D"6386">G=C3=A9rer proprement rollback en =
cas d=E2=80=99erreur</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6387" data-end=3D"6460">
<p data-start=3D"6389" data-end=3D"6460">Toujours remettre auto-commit =C3=
=A0 <code data-start=3D"6421" data-end=3D"6427">true</code> apr=C3=A8s une =
transaction manuelle</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6461" data-end=3D"6543">
<p data-start=3D"6463" data-end=3D"6543">Utiliser des <strong data-start=3D=
"6476" data-end=3D"6490">savepoints</strong> pour contr=C3=B4ler finement l=
es annulations partielles</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6544" data-end=3D"6612">
<p data-start=3D"6546" data-end=3D"6612">Toujours fermer statements et resu=
ltsets avec try-with-resources</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6613" data-end=3D"6683">
<p data-start=3D"6615" data-end=3D"6683">Traiter et logger pr=C3=A9cis=C3=
=A9ment les exceptions (SQLState, errorCode)</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6684" data-end=3D"6782">
<p data-start=3D"6686" data-end=3D"6782">Dans un environnement multi-thread=
=C3=A9, s=E2=80=99assurer que la connexion n=E2=80=99est pas partag=C3=A9e =
entre threads</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"6784" data-end=3D"6787">
