<hr data-start=3D"2296" data-end=3D"2299">
<h3 data-start=3D"2301" data-end=3D"2332">1.3 Pourquoi utiliser JWT ?</h3>
<ul data-start=3D"2334" data-end=3D"2675">
<li data-start=3D"2334" data-end=3D"2450">
<p data-start=3D"2336" data-end=3D"2450"><strong data-start=3D"2336" data-e=
nd=3D"2349">Stateless</strong> : le serveur n=E2=80=99a pas besoin de stock=
er les sessions, le token contient les informations n=C3=A9cessaires.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2451" data-end=3D"2548">
<p data-start=3D"2453" data-end=3D"2548"><strong data-start=3D"2453" data-e=
nd=3D"2473">Interop=C3=A9rabilit=C3=A9</strong> : standard JSON, facile =C3=
=A0 utiliser sur diff=C3=A9rents langages et plateformes.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2549" data-end=3D"2614">
<p data-start=3D"2551" data-end=3D"2614"><strong data-start=3D"2551" data-e=
nd=3D"2566">Scalabilit=C3=A9</strong> : pas besoin de partager l=E2=80=99=
=C3=A9tat entre serveurs.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2615" data-end=3D"2675">
<p data-start=3D"2617" data-end=3D"2675"><strong data-start=3D"2617" data-e=
nd=3D"2629">S=C3=A9curit=C3=A9</strong> : signature assurant l=E2=80=99int=
=C3=A9grit=C3=A9 des donn=C3=A9es.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"2677" data-end=3D"2680">
<h2 data-start=3D"2682" data-end=3D"2718">2. Principes de s=C3=A9curit=C3=
=A9 avec JWT</h2>
<h3 data-start=3D"2720" data-end=3D"2752">2.1 Signature vs chiffrement</h3>
<ul data-start=3D"2754" data-end=3D"2884">
<li data-start=3D"2754" data-end=3D"2814">
<p data-start=3D"2756" data-end=3D"2814"><strong data-start=3D"2756" data-e=
nd=3D"2769">Signature</strong> : garantit que le token n=E2=80=99a pas =C3=
=A9t=C3=A9 modifi=C3=A9.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2815" data-end=3D"2884">
<p data-start=3D"2817" data-end=3D"2884"><strong data-start=3D"2817" data-e=
nd=3D"2832">Chiffrement</strong> : optionnel, prot=C3=A8ge la confidentiali=
t=C3=A9 du contenu.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start=3D"2886" data-end=3D"2909">2.2 Types de tokens</h3>
<ul data-start=3D"2911" data-end=3D"3057">
<li data-start=3D"2911" data-end=3D"2981">
<p data-start=3D"2913" data-end=3D"2981"><strong data-start=3D"2913" data-e=
nd=3D"2929">Access Token</strong> : court terme, utilis=C3=A9 pour acc=C3=
=A9der aux ressources.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2982" data-end=3D"3057">
<p data-start=3D"2984" data-end=3D"3057"><strong data-start=3D"2984" data-e=
nd=3D"3001">Refresh Token</strong> : plus long terme, permet de r=C3=A9g=C3=
=A9n=C3=A9rer un access token.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"3059" data-end=3D"3062">
<h2 data-start=3D"3064" data-end=3D"3095">3. JWT dans le contexte Java</h2>
