<hr data-start=3D"6634" data-end=3D"6637">
<h2 data-start=3D"6639" data-end=3D"6671">9. Cross-Site Scripting (XSS)</h2=
>
<h3 data-start=3D"6673" data-end=3D"6692">9.1 Description</h3>
<p data-start=3D"6694" data-end=3D"6778">Injection de scripts malveillants =
dans des pages web vues par d=E2=80=99autres utilisateurs.</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"6780" data-end=3D"6796">9.2 Exemples</h3>
<ul data-start=3D"6798" data-end=3D"6866">
<li data-start=3D"6798" data-end=3D"6866">
<p data-start=3D"6800" data-end=3D"6866">Affichage de donn=C3=A9es utilisat=
eurs non filtr=C3=A9es dans JSP/Thymeleaf.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start=3D"6868" data-end=3D"6886">9.3 Pr=C3=A9vention</h3>
<ul data-start=3D"6888" data-end=3D"7068">
<li data-start=3D"6888" data-end=3D"6966">
<p data-start=3D"6890" data-end=3D"6966">=C3=89chapper les sorties (ex : <c=
ode data-start=3D"6917" data-end=3D"6951">${#strings.escapeHtml(variable)}<=
/code> en Thymeleaf).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6967" data-end=3D"7040">
<p data-start=3D"6969" data-end=3D"7040">Utiliser des biblioth=C3=A8ques de=
 sanitization (OWASP Java HTML Sanitizer).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"7041" data-end=3D"7068">
<p data-start=3D"7043" data-end=3D"7068">Utiliser des headers CSP.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"7070" data-end=3D"7073">
<h2 data-start=3D"7075" data-end=3D"7138">10. Insecure Deserialization (D=
=C3=A9s=C3=A9rialisation non s=C3=A9curis=C3=A9e)</h2>
<h3 data-start=3D"7140" data-end=3D"7160">10.1 Description</h3>
<p data-start=3D"7162" data-end=3D"7250">La d=C3=A9s=C3=A9rialisation d=E2=
=80=99objets non fiables peut conduire =C3=A0 l=E2=80=99ex=C3=A9cution de c=
ode malveillant.</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"7252" data-end=3D"7276">10.2 Risques en Java</h3>
<ul data-start=3D"7278" data-end=3D"7390">
<li data-start=3D"7278" data-end=3D"7353">
<p data-start=3D"7280" data-end=3D"7353">Utilisation de la s=C3=A9rialisati=
on Java standard avec des donn=C3=A9es non s=C3=BBres.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"7354" data-end=3D"7390">
<p data-start=3D"7356" data-end=3D"7390">Biblioth=C3=A8ques tierces vuln=C3=
=A9rables.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start=3D"7392" data-end=3D"7411">10.3 Pr=C3=A9vention</h3>
<ul data-start=3D"7413" data-end=3D"7568">
<li data-start=3D"7413" data-end=3D"7464">
<p data-start=3D"7415" data-end=3D"7464">=C3=89viter la d=C3=A9s=C3=A9riali=
sation de donn=C3=A9es non fiables.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"7465" data-end=3D"7505">
<p data-start=3D"7467" data-end=3D"7505">Utiliser des biblioth=C3=A8ques s=
=C3=A9curis=C3=A9es.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"7506" data-end=3D"7568">
<p data-start=3D"7508" data-end=3D"7568">Mettre en place des listes blanche=
s pour classes autoris=C3=A9es.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"7570" data-end=3D"7573">
<h2 data-start=3D"7575" data-end=3D"7625">11. Using Components with Known V=
ulnerabilities</h2>
<h3 data-start=3D"7627" data-end=3D"7644">11.1 Probl=C3=A8me</h3>
<p data-start=3D"7646" data-end=3D"7730">Utiliser des biblioth=C3=A8ques av=
ec des vuln=C3=A9rabilit=C3=A9s connues expose votre application.</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"7732" data-end=3D"7751">11.2 Pr=C3=A9vention</h3>
<ul data-start=3D"7753" data-end=3D"7871">
<li data-start=3D"7753" data-end=3D"7801">
<p data-start=3D"7755" data-end=3D"7801">Garder les d=C3=A9pendances =C3=A0=
 jour (Maven, Gradle).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"7802" data-end=3D"7871">
<p data-start=3D"7804" data-end=3D"7871">Scanner avec des outils comme <str=
ong data-start=3D"7834" data-end=3D"7860">OWASP Dependency-Check</strong>, =
<strong data-start=3D"7862" data-end=3D"7870">Snyk</strong>.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"7873" data-end=3D"7876">
<h2 data-start=3D"7878" data-end=3D"7918">12. Insufficient Logging &amp; Mo=
nitoring</h2>
<h3 data-start=3D"7920" data-end=3D"7939">12.1 Importance</h3>
<p data-start=3D"7941" data-end=3D"8017">Sans logs et surveillance efficace=
s, les attaques peuvent passer inaper=C3=A7ues.</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"8019" data-end=3D"8044">12.2 Bonnes pratiques</h3>
<ul data-start=3D"8046" data-end=3D"8208">
<li data-start=3D"8046" data-end=3D"8123">
<p data-start=3D"8048" data-end=3D"8123">Logger les =C3=A9v=C3=A9nements cr=
itiques (=C3=A9checs de connexion, acc=C3=A8s non autoris=C3=A9s).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"8124" data-end=3D"8168">
<p data-start=3D"8126" data-end=3D"8168">Prot=C3=A9ger les logs contre tout=
e alt=C3=A9ration.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"8169" data-end=3D"8208">
<p data-start=3D"8171" data-end=3D"8208">Mettre en place un syst=C3=A8me d=
=E2=80=99alertes.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"8210" data-end=3D"8213">
<h2 data-start=3D"8215" data-end=3D"8285">13. Bonnes pratiques et outils po=
ur s=C3=A9curiser vos applications Java</h2>
<ul data-start=3D"8287" data-end=3D"8609">
<li data-start=3D"8287" data-end=3D"8365">
<p data-start=3D"8289" data-end=3D"8365">Utiliser <strong data-start=3D"829=
8" data-end=3D"8317">Spring Security</strong> pour les contr=C3=B4les d=E2=
=80=99acc=C3=A8s et authentification.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"8366" data-end=3D"8420">
<p data-start=3D"8368" data-end=3D"8420">Valider et nettoyer toutes les ent=
r=C3=A9es utilisateurs.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"8421" data-end=3D"8494">
<p data-start=3D"8423" data-end=3D"8494">Utiliser des outils de test de s=
=C3=A9curit=C3=A9 : <strong data-start=3D"8465" data-end=3D"8478">SonarQube=
</strong>, <strong data-start=3D"8480" data-end=3D"8493">OWASP ZAP</strong>=
.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"8495" data-end=3D"8561">
<p data-start=3D"8497" data-end=3D"8561">Adopter des politiques de s=C3=A9c=
urit=C3=A9 claires (CORS, CSP, headers).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"8562" data-end=3D"8609">
<p data-start=3D"8564" data-end=3D"8609">Former les =C3=A9quipes au d=C3=A9=
veloppement s=C3=A9curis=C3=A9.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"8611" data-end=3D"8614">
<h2 data-start=3D"8616" data-end=3D"8658">14. =C3=89tudes de cas et exemple=
s pratiques</h2>
<ul data-start=3D"8660" data-end=3D"8877">
<li data-start=3D"8660" data-end=3D"8709">
